From 4dd95c3e2c1a325b5766930911ce21899dd2469b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 04:28:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?phlink:=20phase=205-03=20=E2=80=94=20wire=20adb?=
 =?UTF-8?q?lock=20URLLoaderThrottle=20into=20ChromeContentBrowserClient?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a blink::URLLoaderThrottle that consults a process-global
phlink::adblock::Engine and cancels matching loads with
ERR_BLOCKED_BY_CLIENT. Inserted at the head of
ChromeContentBrowserClient::CreateURLLoaderThrottles so blocked
requests short-circuit before any other throttle does work.

- chrome/browser/phlink/adblock/engine_provider.{h,cc}: process-wide
  singleton holding the live Engine. Lazy init with empty rules in
  v1; plan 5-04 will seed the bundled lists. std::mutex (not
  base::Lock) so the .h has no transitive partition_alloc dep.
- chrome/browser/phlink/adblock/phlink_adblock_throttle.{h,cc}:
  WillStartRequest + WillRedirectRequest map RequestDestination to
  adblock-rust's request-type vocabulary, fail open on malformed
  URLs and non-HTTP(S) schemes, and honor exception ($@@) hits.
- chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc: prepend the
  adblock throttle to the result vector.
- chrome/browser/BUILD.gn: pull in :phlink_adblock from the
  static_library("browser") deps.
- chrome/browser/phlink/adblock/BUILD.gn: drop testonly from the
  ffi + source_set targets so they can ship into chrome.
- third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml +
  regenerated BUILD.gn files: promote adblock, aho-corasick, regex,
  regex-automata, psl, psl-types out of Group::Test so the engine
  links into chrome (non-testonly).
- phlink_adblock_unittest.cc: 2 new EngineProvider tests
  (singleton stability + SetEngineFromRulesForTesting swap).

Verified:
- ./out/Default/phlink_adblock_unittests → 6/6 SUCCESS.
- autoninja chrome → Build Succeeded.

Refs PRD §6 (adblock subsystem) and ADBL-01.
